{
  "id": "Compound::DB00951 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Isoniazid appears to interact with Cyp2d6 through a series of mechanistic pathways involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Isoniazid binds to Cyp2a6 and Cyp1a2, which are both involved in the oxidation of arachidonic acid. This binding may inhibit the enzymatic activity of these cytochromes, which in turn affects the production of arachidonic acid epoxygenase and monooxygenase activities. These activities are ultimately linked to Cyp2d6, indicating a potential role for Isoniazid in modulating Cyp2d6 function. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains partially elucidated. The observed effects on arachidonic acid metabolism may have implications for drug metabolism and toxicity, particularly in the context of Cyp2d6's role in drug activation and detoxification.",
